Unreleased:
 - Replaced the legacy Python implementation with a Rust port. The Rust
   binary is now the canonical dduper at /usr/sbin/dduper.
 - Removed dependencies on numpy and PTable (now using std HashMap/HashSet
   and the comfy-table crate).
 - Post-dedupe validation now performs a real SHA256 content comparison
   between the destination and its backup, where the previous Python
   implementation only compared stat info.
 - --verbose short flag moved from -V to -v; -V/--version is now the
   standard clap-provided version flag.

v0.04: 18-09-2020
 - Added xxhash64, blake2, sha256 support
